A realistic hackathon build should prioritize a complete vertical slice rather than a broad feature set. The team should build one polished scenario end-to-end, plus a second scenario as evidence of extensibility.

| Day / Phase | Build target | Deliverable |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Phase 1: Skeleton** | Web UI, backend routes, scenario JSON, profile form. | User can start a scenario and see preview. |
| **Phase 2: Role-play** | Character/chat interface, transcript state, safety checks. | User can role-play a short conversation. |
| **Phase 3: Evaluation** | Rubric evaluator and feedback display. | User receives one strength and one next step. |
| **Phase 4: Runway replay** | Replay Director and Runway media adapter. | User can generate and view Replay Lens clip. |
| **Phase 5: Retry and progress** | Second attempt comparison and social-validity rating. | Demo shows adaptive loop and respectful feedback. |
| **Phase 6: Polish** | Loading states, captions, privacy copy, demo script. | Hackathon-ready story and reliable fallback media. |

