## 16. Production considerations

A real ScenarioLab product would need deeper privacy, security, and validation work. The system might process highly sensitive conversations, so production should include encryption at rest, strict access control, data-retention policies, consent records, export/delete workflows, moderation logs, and human review. If the product is used by schools, clinics, minors, or healthcare-adjacent organizations, legal and compliance review becomes mandatory.

| Area | Production need |
| --- | --- |
| **Security** | Encrypted storage, secret management, signed media URLs, audit logs, least-privilege roles. |
| **Privacy** | Retention controls, deletion workflows, data export, consent history, minimized raw media storage. |
| **Clinical boundary** | Clear disclaimers, professional review, crisis policies, and no diagnostic claims. |
| **Participatory design** | Autistic advisors reviewing language, scenarios, rubrics, and feedback tone. |
| **Validation** | Social-validity study first; pilot study second; real-world transfer study only with appropriate oversight. |
| **Model governance** | Prompt/version tracking, evaluation logs, red-team testing, bias review, fallback behavior. |

## 17. Key technical risks

The biggest technical risk is not whether Runway can generate media. It is whether the app can reliably orchestrate media generation inside a structured, respectful, scientifically humble product loop. The second major risk is latency: generated replay clips may take long enough that the UX needs asynchronous status and fallback storyboards.

| Risk | Mitigation |
| --- | --- |
| **Runway task latency disrupts flow** | Show storyboard immediately, poll job asynchronously, notify user when video is ready. |
| **Character availability or API limitations** | Use text chat plus pre-generated avatar clips as fallback. |
| **Evaluator gives harmful or narrow feedback** | Constrain to rubric, run feedback rewriter, add social-validity flagging. |
| **Generated replay misrepresents scenario** | Frame as possible interpretation; use curated prompts; allow user to reject or flag. |
| **Privacy concerns** | Store structured summaries by default; make raw transcript retention opt-in. |
| **Overclaiming scientific efficacy** | Use non-clinical wording and measure social validity before outcomes. |

